Back by popular demand, we are bringing collision between cabbies for that extra bit of spice.

We've gathered loads of amazing feedback over the past month at various in-person events and we've listened to you. Thank you for being there, playing and showing your love for Cabbie! and helping make it even more fun!

Here's a list with all the major 1.5 changes and the previous 1.4 changes:

[list]
[*] Default Taxi level time shortened to 2:30;
[*] Cab collision enabled;
[*] Going through a menu before launching Steam when pressing the Wishlist button;
[*] Celebration fireworks when defeating Boss and on podiums;
[*] Ping system that triggers when attemping to use an empty battery or if attempting to deliver at the wrong address;
[*] Better visibility for net in level 1;
[*] With levels being shorter, we've halved the scores and re-set the save game as the highscore will not be achievable anymore.
[/list]

Bug fixes:
[list]
[*] Missing image on license;
[*] Going into the game as Cabbie when having chosen other characters;
[/list]
We are aware of a few more bugs and we will do a small bug-fix update very soon.

We're hoping these changes will add much more chaos and more importantly, MORE FUN!

Lots of love,
Cabbie's Buddies ːsteamhappyː

Hi there Cabbies! We're excited to share with you a BIG Cabbie! update in Demo 1.2, right on time for Steam Co-Op fest and Yorkshire Games Festival UK next week. Better messaging, even MORE SHEEP, a new character customisation option and fireworks!!

We're currently looking to improve the Boss and End-Match celebration experience along with some final few bugs. Demo 1.3 will the be final major update to the Demo before we go back and finish the rest of the game!

So please if you have any feedback do let us know, we want to make Cabbie! a fun experience for everyone.
Also, please feel free to share in-game footage and screenshots however you like.

This being said, jump right in to check out the updates or read the detailed list below.

Happy cabbying!

[previewyoutube=wRMsnHqzD6A;full][/previewyoutube]

Updates:
[list]
[*] Firework celebration for goal scorers;
[*] Clearer labels on the levels you have unlocked to show what is 'new';
[*] A better and clearer character select menu showing the names of the characters;
[*] The ability to change the base paint colour of your character from the initial four character colours;
[*] Training has two extra steps teaching you about the world being destructible and how to use your zap to stop Sheeplets;
[*] Training now displays the number of stages and ticks them off as you progress;
[*] Sheeplets are now in world 1 level 1 to add to the overall challenge of the first level experience;
[*] Scoring is now clearer with a new and improved UI and celebration effect;
[*] Fines are now clearer with a new and improved UI element;
[*] Pickups now have a clear effect when you collect them;
[*] Interaction button prompt changed to a yellow progress bar for clarity.
[/list]

Bug fixes:
[list]
[*] You will no longer slide along the floor when completing a level after the timer;
[*] Meeplets no longer appear in the middle of the training level when they exit their buildings;
[*] Some control icons in the training level that were too small are now larger;
[*] Intro timer and end of match timer are now fixed in terms of the timing and the associated sound effects;
[*] Your character and control selections no longer reset if a player leaves when in character select;
[*] Meeplets no longer overlap when they exit a building at the same time;
[*] Re-enabled camera shake for the boss fight when it slams into the ground;
[*] Join button in character select no longer visible when all four players join.
[/list]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/45353752/6645ede34e8c35764c3a9d1f4f1d07feb56ce658.jpg[/img]

Hi everyone,

We're very grateful for everyone that's wishlisted and played our demo so far.

Based on initial feedback we're doing a few updates to our demo to improve your play experience.

In this update we've done the following:

UI:
[list]
[*] Added input info to the pause menu to highlight all control schemes;
[*] Added a Menu prompt to the level select UI;
[*] Improved tutorial prompts;
[*] Improved coin animation when gaining score;
[*] Added version number;
[/list]

Vehicle:
[list]
[*] Matching reverse speed with acceleration speed;
[*] Improved handbreak turn;
[/list]

Controls:
[list]
[*] In acceleration mode, slowing down the car faster for better control;
[/list]

Sheeplets:
[list]
[*] Spawning sheeplets less often;
[/list]

Meeplets:
[list]
[*] More vivid colours;
[/list]

Hoping these updates will help everyone get those busy meeplets to where they need to go. 

Wishlist and stay tuned for more updates.
